From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:41:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: a rune's target stops flickering, its ID readback
 waiting for the GPU; built, untested on console

FPS++'s deferred readbacks let GX2DrawDone return before a texture readback has finished. The
results the game reads a frame later are fine with that, but gfx::IDAnalyzer, which picks the
target under a rune's reticle, reads its ID readback and coverage query as it uses them: it sees a
stale or empty ID, so the camera rune's target name blinks and jumps between two screen positions
and its detection beep repeats. Its query now asks for four full-sync draw-dones first; every
other readback stays deferred.

This is upstream BetterVR 1.0.2's fix (02bcbe6, "Stop rune targets from flickering"), which the
1.0.0 pin predates; drop this patch when the pin moves to 1.0.2.

A console test: the camera rune aimed at a landmark must keep one name in one place, beep once,
and still take a photo.
---
 .../Mods/FPS++/patch_DeferredReadbacks.asm               | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/FPS++/patch_DeferredReadbacks.asm b/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/FPS++/patch_DeferredReadbacks.asm
index 7f12911..29d6c41 100644
--- a/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/FPS++/patch_DeferredReadbacks.asm
+++ b/resources/graphicPacks/BreathOfTheWild/Mods/FPS++/patch_DeferredReadbacks.asm
@@ -79,6 +79,15 @@ blr
 0x036E9EF0 = bla bakeTerrainColorUnorm ; Terrain colour bake, RGBA8
 0x036E9F0C = bla bakeTerrainColorFloat ; Terrain colour bake, RGBA32F
 
+; rune targeting reads its ID readback and coverage query a frame later, deferring them made the target flicker
+idAnalyzerQueryBegin:
+lis r11, fullSyncDrawDones@ha
+li r12, 4
+stw r12, fullSyncDrawDones@l(r11)
+ba import.gx2.GX2QueryBegin
+
+0x038B29BC = bla idAnalyzerQueryBegin ; gfx::IDAnalyzer
+
 ; Cemu reports a GPU occlusion query that hasn't finished as having 0 samples, which would hide objects.
 ; A CPU query reports that it isn't ready yet instead, which the game handles. Also fixes distant NPCs stuttering
 ; in OpenGL with "Full sync at GX2DrawDone()" turned off.
